% Protected local ChatGPT credentials
Own pdd/chatgpt_credentials.py. Export CredentialError(code) and CredentialStore(root=None).
R1: Default ~/.pdd/chatgpt. Use 0700 directories, 0600 files, atomic replace plus fsync.
Reject symlinks, foreign owners, unsafe permissions. Only Python built-ins.
R2: One stable urn:uuid UUIDv4 per host, generated under cross-process flock.
Account keys hash verified issuer, subject and issued client_id; workspaces stay separate.
R3: Serialize sign-in replacement, refresh and export with per-account flock. summary
returns only method/state/accountKey/label/errorCode/updatedAt. No automatic activation.
R4: Validate import metadata and credential shape; preserve destination host ID.
Import selected registration only. Source export is fenced before SSH and stays fenced
on uncertainty. Successful acknowledgement clears source tokens. VM owns later refresh.
R5: Tokens, grant, expiry, earliest_refresh_at and refresh owner are replaced together.
Never log credentials, paths or raw exceptions. Use safe error codes.
R6: usage(key, exclusive=False) is a separate crash-released flock. Runtime children
share read leases. Transfer/import use an exclusive nonblocking lease and fail while
any reader runs. Credential refresh locking remains short and independent.
